<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">David Lloyd George</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1863">1863</a>–<a href="/years/1945">1945</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Lloyd George</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Lloyd George was a Welsh Liberal politician and Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from 1916 to 1922. Member of Parliament for Caernarvon Boroughs for 55 years, he became Chancellor of the Exchequer in 1908 and proposed taxes on land ownership and high incomes in the People's Budget of 1909 to fund welfare reforms; its rejection by the House of Lords led to a constitutional crisis resolved by the Parliament Act 1911. His budget, the National Insurance Act 1911 and other measures helped establish the modern welfare state. He led the country through the later years of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, took part in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris-peace-conference-1919-1920">Paris Peace Conference</a> and negotiated the establishment of the Irish Free State.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/david-lloyd-george.jpg" alt="David Lloyd George" width="330" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harris &amp; Ewing · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:David_Lloyd_George.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
